<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Rep max YTM for Aug 5, 5yr auction 12.35 pct.</title>
<headline>Czech Rep max YTM for Aug 5, 5yr auction 12.35 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech National Bank said on Tuesday that its August 5 auction of five-year state bonds will have a maximum acceptable yield to maturity (YTM) on bids of 12.35 percent.  </p>
<p>BONDS OF THE CZECH REPUBLIC  (18TH ISSUE) 1997-2000</p>
<p>  ISIN:		CZ 0001000491</p>
<p>  ISSUER:	    FINANCE MINISTRY ON BEHALF OF THE CZECH REP.</p>
<p>  AMOUNT:	    CZK 5 BLN</p>
<p>  NOMINAL VALUE:   CZK 10,000</p>
<p>  BOND TYPE:	 BEARER</p>
<p>  ISSUE DATE:	AUGUST 15, 1997</p>
<p>  MATURITY DATE:   AUGUST 15, 2002</p>
<p>  MATURITY:	  FIVE YEARS</p>
<p>  COUPON:	    DETERMINED AT AUCTION BY MULTIPLE PRICE</p>
<p>			 (AMERICAN) AUCTION AS AVERAGE YTM</p>
<p>COUPON PAY</p>
<p>  FREQUENCY:	 ANNUALLY</p>
<p>  EX-COUPON:	 JULY 15</p>
<p>INTEREST</p>
<p>  INCOME TAX:	ACCORDING TO CZECH LAW (PRESENTLY 25 PCT)</p>
<p>MAXIMUM</p>
<p>ACCEPTABLE YTM:  12.35 PCT p.a.</p>
<p>DEADLINE FOR</p>
<p>  BIDDING:	   AUGUST 4, 12.00 p.m. (1000 GMT)</p>
<p>  AUCTION DATE:    AUGUST 5</p>
<p>ADMINISTRATOR</p>
<p>(PAYING AGENT):  INVESTICNI A POSTOVNI BANKA A.S.</p>
<p>  LATEST S&amp;P:	A</p>
<p>LATEST MOODY'S:  Baa1</p>
<p>-- John Mastrini, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
